! PROFN2 is PROFN2(NSM) in trx (see trx/trparm.f90's '&TR ... PROFN1,PROFN2,PROFN3:NSM'),
! but a bare scalar in kyoshimi tr, where one value covers every species.  Writing one
! value here would set species 1 only and leave 2..4 at trx/trinit.f90's 0.5, NOT the
! kyoshimi deck's meaning and breaks quasineutrality.  Spell all NSMAX values out.
